## Monitor / Don't Build Yet

Keep these documented, but do not spend development time on them unless they become real customer problems.

- [ ] **Concurrent Checkout tabs.** Two simultaneous Checkout sessions could theoretically create duplicate subscriptions on one Stripe customer. Low probability; support can refund the duplicate. Add server-side idempotency/open-session protection only if this actually occurs.

- [ ] **Static paid assets are publicly fetchable.** Game scripts under `/resource/...` return `200` without authentication. This matches the legacy architecture; the paywall protects access through game/share codes rather than file secrecy. Revisit only if product positioning changes.


